integrationNeeds:
main.js changes, in order. Nothing needs to be added to the render path — clouds.js:797-798 already calls lights.prepare() and lights.writeUniforms() inside _writeCameraUniforms, once per drawn frame.

1. IMPORT (near main.js:18, beside the CloudSystem import):
   import { shipLamp, thrusterPlume } from './render/lights.js';

2. CONSTRUCT, once, after `const clouds = new CloudSystem(...)` at main.js:63 and after `const ship = new Flight({ rng })` at :67:
   const lampId  = clouds.lights.add(shipLamp());
   const plumeId = clouds.lights.add(thrusterPlume());
   const LAMP_FWD = new THREE.Vector3();   // module-scope scratch, like TURB at :152
   const LAMP_POS = new THREE.Vector3();
   let lampOn = true;                       // bind to a key via input/controls later

3. PER FIXED STEP, inside update(dt) at main.js:121, AFTER ship.step(dt) (:142) and BEFORE clouds.update(dt, camera) (:147) so the registry sees this step's pose:
   LAMP_FWD.copy(ship.forward);                    // Flight exposes `get forward()` at flight.js:162
   LAMP_POS.copy(ship.position).addScaledVector(LAMP_FWD, 2.0);
   clouds.lights.set(lampId, {
     position:  [LAMP_POS.x, LAMP_POS.y, LAMP_POS.z],
     direction: [LAMP_FWD.x, LAMP_FWD.y, LAMP_FWD.z],
     on: lampOn,
   });
   LAMP_POS.copy(ship.position).addScaledVector(LAMP_FWD, -3.0);
   clouds.lights.set(plumeId, {
     position:  [LAMP_POS.x, LAMP_POS.y, LAMP_POS.z],
     direction: [-LAMP_FWD.x, -LAMP_FWD.y, -LAMP_FWD.z],
     intensity: 1.5 * (0.15 + 0.85 * ship.throttleSmoothed),   // ship.throttleSmoothed, flight.js:142
     on: ship.throttleSmoothed > 0.01,
   });

   MANDATORY: `direction` must never be all zeros. A zero vector survives normalisation (lights.js:146) and the spot goes silently black while still counting toward signature() — see the bug list. Do not seed it from an unpopulated Vector3.

4. NO RENDER CALL. Do not call prepare() or writeUniforms() from main.js; clouds.js owns that and calling it twice would double-write the uniforms.

5. EXPOSE, in the globalThis.GAME literal at main.js:205:
     lights: clouds.lights,
   and add `lights ${JSON.stringify(clouds.lights.debugSummary().keys)}` to the diag string at main.js:194 so a capture can state which lights were live.

6. BEFORE ANY OF THIS, cut the light budget. With MAX_MARCH_LIGHTS at 8 the volumetric pass measures 15.2 ms against a 7 ms budget once eight lights are in range. Two ship lights are affordable (measured 4.18 ms at n=1); the third light already exceeds budget at 7.49 ms. Set MAX_MARCH_LIGHTS to 3 in lights.js:47 before wiring, or the first storm cell that fires next to the ship blows the frame.

7. SIGNATURE, separate task: signature.js does not import lights.js and its photic channel is in lumens (SIG.caps.photic 60000, exposureRef 40000) while lights.signature() returns radiance (~6.5 for lamp + plume). The ShipSystems class its _photic() reads from does not exist in the repo. Wiring these together needs a MEASURED radiance-to-lumen conversion against the anchor table in signature.js — not a guessed constant.
